venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/

# Local copy of the UNCLEANED source dataset, pulled from the private
# HF repo (prss-majorproject-37/Handwritten-AnswerScripts-MajorProject).
# Real student pages - names, USNs, signatures, marks - so never
# tracked. Re-fetch with:
#   huggingface-cli download --repo-type dataset \
#     prss-majorproject-37/Handwritten-AnswerScripts-MajorProject \
#     --local-dir dataset
dataset/

# Secrets - never commit the Hugging Face token
.env

# Student answer scripts contain personal data: names, USNs, signatures
# and marks. The source dataset is a PRIVATE Hugging Face repo and the
# converted copies must not enter git history either.
#
# modules/01_prepare/ is organised as numbered per-stage folders
# (01_deskew/, 02_crop/, 03_tone/), each with its own
# input/output/preview - all of which hold real page images or point at
# them, so every stage is covered by one glob rather than adding a line
# per stage.
# No trailing slash: a stage's input/ is sometimes a real directory and
# sometimes a symlink to the previous stage's output. A trailing slash
# matches only directories, which would leave the symlink form tracked -
# and it points into gitignored preprocessing_legacy/, so it would be a
# broken link for anyone else cloning.
# Two depths, because modules differ in shape: 01_prepare holds
# numbered sub-stages (modules/01_prepare/03_tone/output) while
# 02_segment is flat (modules/02_segment/output).
# check/ is 06_evaluation's registration renders - annotated real pages,
# same reason as annotated/ and preview/.
# segmentation/ is 07_reconstruct's junction into 02_segment/output -
# geometry, not images, but it is regenerated by segment.py and a
# junction target should never be tracked either way.
modules/*/input
modules/*/output
modules/*/preview
modules/*/annotated
modules/*/crops
modules/*/check
modules/*/segmentation
modules/*/*/input
modules/*/*/output
modules/*/*/preview
modules/*/*/annotated
modules/*/*/crops
modules/*/*/check
modules/01_prepare/students.csv

# The annotation sample points at those same pages, and the review
# sheets rendered from them are readable images of real answer scripts.
# The manifest and the labels themselves are safe to track - they carry
# geometry, not content - so they are deliberately NOT ignored.
annotation/images/
annotation/review/
annotation/preannotations/
annotation/dataset/
annotation/runs/
annotation/review_labels/
annotation/cloud_upload/
annotation/annotated/
annotation/overnight.log

# Ultralytics defaults here if a script forgets to set `project`
runs/
*.pt
annotation/remap_check/
annotation/images_cleaned/
annotation/dataset_clean/
annotation/segmented/
annotation/seg_run.log

# 07_reconstruct: marker crops are cut from real answer scripts, and the
# label sheets render them in bulk. Geometry and labels are safe; the
# pixels are not. The trained weights stay out too - they are derived
# from student handwriting and are large.
modules/*/markers

# 06_evaluation: a transcription IS the student's answer, and predictions
# are the same text with errors in it. The scoring code and the page
# selection are safe to track; what is written on the pages is not.
modules/*/ground_truth
modules/*/predictions
# 04_ocr: line crops, their transcriptions, and any tuned checkpoint are
# all derived from real answer scripts. The scripts that build them are
# tracked; the data and weights are not.
modules/*/finetune
# 04_ocr: the upload batches ARE the scanned pages, just zipped for
# transport to a GPU. They must never enter git.
modules/*/upload
# Hand-made ground truth at the repo root. A transcription IS the
# student answer, so it stays local like every other page artefact.
/ground_truth/

# Answer keys. The extracted cie*.json IS repo content - it is the
# marking scheme in machine-readable form and everything in 04_evaluate
# depends on it. The 21MB of page renders beside it are a derived
# artefact of make_grader_notebook's extraction step and rebuild from the
# PDFs in seconds, so they stay out.
modules/04_evaluate/keys/pages/

# experiments/ follows the same rule as modules/: anything named
# upload/ or output/ under an experiment holds real page images, or is
# derived directly from them. The diagram review sheet is the sharpest
# case - review.html embeds base64 crops of student handwriting inline,
# so it is a page image wearing a text file's extension and weighs
# 2.6 MB. Hand-authored labels (labels.py) and code stay tracked.
experiments/*/upload
experiments/*/output
experiments/*/output_*

# 02_read: kaggle_run.py stages a copy of the corpus here before pushing
# it to a private Kaggle dataset, so kaggle/dataset/pages holds real
# scanned pages and kaggle/output holds the transcriptions that come
# back - a transcription IS the student's answer. The generated kernel
# beside them is safe, but it is not worth a narrower glob: everything
# under this directory is regenerated by kaggle_run.py in seconds.
# This is the same trap that staged 322MB of page zips once, one
# directory over.
modules/*/kaggle

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Part 1's delivered corpus. 187MB, 1,361 files, and every one of them
# is a real student's transcribed answer or a crop of their page. It
# arrived as a folder rather than through the dataset/ path above, so
# none of the rules further up caught it - `git add -A` would have
# staged the lot.
#
# Nothing needs it in git: Pranay produced it and already holds it, and
# the evaluation half reaches it by path rather than by copy. Point
# MPE_HANDOFF at wherever it lives on your machine.
handoff_Pranay/

# The department's answer schemes, 7.3MB of scanned PDF. They are the
# faculty's material, not ours to publish, and the same escape hatch
# applies - MPE_SCHEMES.
answer_keys/

# Local scratch for the worklist tool.
.worklist.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# extra/ - everything from our side of Iter1, archived out of the way so
# the handoff is just the two evaluation folders.
#
# THIS BLOCK IS LOAD-BEARING. Every rule above that names `modules/...`
# or `experiments/...` is anchored to the repo root, so the moment those
# two folders moved under extra/ each of those rules stopped matching -
# and every one of them exists to keep real student pages out of git.
# The move alone would have un-ignored page images, transcriptions,
# predictions and upload zips in one commit.
#
# These are the same rules re-anchored with `**`, which matches at any
# depth and so survives the next move too.
extra/**/input/
extra/**/output/
extra/**/output_*/
extra/**/preview/
extra/**/annotated/
extra/**/crops/
extra/**/check/
extra/**/segmentation/
extra/**/markers/
extra/**/ground_truth/
extra/**/predictions/
extra/**/finetune/
extra/**/upload/
extra/**/kaggle/
extra/**/keys/pages/
extra/**/students.csv
extra/**/*.pt

# The evaluation folders keep their own .gitignore, which is relative to
# where it sits and therefore still correct after the move. These are a
# second line only - output/ holds marks that quote students verbatim,
# and a venv is both large and broken the moment it is moved.
Major_Project_Eval/.venv/
Major_Project_Eval/output/
Major_Project_Eval_Local/.venv/
Major_Project_Eval_Local/output/
